  "question": {
    "text": "The point in the interval $[0,2 \\pi]$, where $f(x)=e^x \\sin x$ has maximum slope, is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\pi$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: $f^{\\prime}(x)=e^x(\\sin x+\\cos x)$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& f^{\\prime \\prime}(x)=e^x(\\sin x+\\cos x+\\cos x-\\sin x) \\Rightarrow f^{\\prime \\prime}(x)=e^x \\cos x=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
}